1
00:00:00,497 --> 00:00:02,730
Now I mentioned that in power user mode you

2
00:00:02,746 --> 00:00:05,589
got some extra options here below your

3
00:00:05,654 --> 00:00:06,344
responses.

4
00:00:07,164 --> 00:00:09,332
And not just there, we also got an extra

5
00:00:09,332 --> 00:00:11,003
option here, for example, when we send a

6
00:00:11,003 --> 00:00:11,308
message.

7
00:00:12,320 --> 00:00:13,396
This user button here

8
00:00:13,990 --> 00:00:16,030
is not there in regular user mode.

9
00:00:17,139 --> 00:00:18,761
So what are these options all about?

10
00:00:19,628 --> 00:00:22,311
For example, we got this branch option here.

11
00:00:23,146 --> 00:00:26,070
And this essentially allows you to fork the

12
00:00:26,070 --> 00:00:27,708
chat to create multiple separate

13
00:00:27,708 --> 00:00:30,870
conversations. Simultaneous parallel chat

14
00:00:30,870 --> 00:00:31,560
histories

15
00:00:32,218 --> 00:00:33,325
after a given message.

16
00:00:33,919 --> 00:00:35,556
So for example, if I click this button here,

17
00:00:36,551 --> 00:00:39,873
you'll see that 2 chats are created here.

18
00:00:40,756 --> 00:00:43,388
So it's very similar to duplicate in the

19
00:00:43,388 --> 00:00:45,779
end, where I also duplicate a chat.

20
00:00:46,598 --> 00:00:48,796
It's simply a way for you to have

21
00:00:49,406 --> 00:00:50,080
multiple

22
00:00:50,850 --> 00:00:53,675
parallel chat histories that are based on

23
00:00:53,675 --> 00:00:57,009
the same start of a chat, but then change

24
00:00:57,009 --> 00:00:59,364
from a certain point on. So where you branch

25
00:00:59,493 --> 00:01:01,303
out into different versions of the chat

26
00:01:01,672 --> 00:01:03,578
because you might have different follow-up

27
00:01:03,658 --> 00:01:05,966
questions. So if I got a response by the

28
00:01:05,966 --> 00:01:08,145
model and now I have 2 different follow-up

29
00:01:08,225 --> 00:01:09,939
questions, which I don't want to have in the

30
00:01:09,939 --> 00:01:11,013
same chat history,

31
00:01:11,670 --> 00:01:15,034
I could branch my chat after this message.

32
00:01:15,932 --> 00:01:18,111
We also have continue assistant message,

33
00:01:18,175 --> 00:01:21,684
which is useful if you got a response that

34
00:01:21,684 --> 00:01:22,821
seems cut off.

35
00:01:23,382 --> 00:01:25,369
Now, that's not the case here, but if you

36
00:01:25,369 --> 00:01:28,317
got a super long response, at some point it

37
00:01:28,366 --> 00:01:31,490
may actually be too much for the model to

38
00:01:31,538 --> 00:01:33,814
handle. They have certain limits regarding

39
00:01:33,878 --> 00:01:35,849
the amount of response tokens they can

40
00:01:35,881 --> 00:01:37,163
generate in one go.

41
00:01:37,723 --> 00:01:39,951
And if that happens, if the response is cut

42
00:01:39,951 --> 00:01:41,777
off, you can always click this button to

43
00:01:41,874 --> 00:01:44,373
have the model continue with the generation

44
00:01:44,373 --> 00:01:46,665
and continue generating a response.

45
00:01:47,498 --> 00:01:50,656
Now, regarding the options down here, User

46
00:01:50,945 --> 00:01:52,759
allows you to actually toggle

47
00:01:53,497 --> 00:01:56,162
between the mode of the message you're about

48
00:01:56,162 --> 00:01:58,554
to send. Now, the default is always user

49
00:01:58,554 --> 00:02:00,417
because you are the user of this

50
00:02:00,417 --> 00:02:02,873
application. You are the user interacting

51
00:02:02,905 --> 00:02:06,116
with the AI model. But for advanced use

52
00:02:06,116 --> 00:02:09,921
cases, you also might want to simulate a

53
00:02:09,969 --> 00:02:12,168
certain AI response. You might want to

54
00:02:12,682 --> 00:02:15,604
artificially create a chat history that

55
00:02:15,604 --> 00:02:16,487
never happened.

56
00:02:17,097 --> 00:02:19,057
And you can do that by switching between

57
00:02:19,186 --> 00:02:21,227
roles. So if I create a new chat here,

58
00:02:21,837 --> 00:02:23,749
I could start with an assistant message

59
00:02:24,649 --> 00:02:27,686
which says, hi, I am an assistant

60
00:02:28,682 --> 00:02:28,875
and I

61
00:02:29,566 --> 00:02:31,703
can help you with using

62
00:02:32,602 --> 00:02:34,514
open LLMs locally.

63
00:02:35,993 --> 00:02:38,451
And we could now simulate that the AI sent

64
00:02:38,483 --> 00:02:40,540
back this response even though it never did.

65
00:02:41,616 --> 00:02:44,026
So if I now send this, I still get a

66
00:02:44,026 --> 00:02:46,757
response by the large language model. So it

67
00:02:46,757 --> 00:02:49,905
still treats this as if a regular user sent

68
00:02:49,905 --> 00:02:50,017
it,

69
00:02:50,595 --> 00:02:52,941
but internally this will be stored as an

70
00:02:52,941 --> 00:02:54,980
assistant message, as you also see here.

71
00:02:55,992 --> 00:02:57,791
And that may be interesting for more

72
00:02:57,920 --> 00:03:00,474
advanced use cases where you then, for

73
00:03:00,474 --> 00:03:02,963
example, later down in the chat, you might

74
00:03:02,963 --> 00:03:04,971
wanna ask the model what it can do for you,

75
00:03:05,052 --> 00:03:06,947
and it will refer back to its earlier

76
00:03:06,979 --> 00:03:09,629
responses, including responses that it

77
00:03:09,710 --> 00:03:12,344
actually never gave you, but that were faked

78
00:03:12,376 --> 00:03:13,629
by you by assigning such

79
00:03:14,384 --> 00:03:15,154
a fake role.

80
00:03:16,471 --> 00:03:19,089
Now, this is definitely a niche feature. I

81
00:03:19,122 --> 00:03:21,129
just wanted to mention it since this button

82
00:03:21,129 --> 00:03:21,482
is here.

83
00:03:22,253 --> 00:03:24,470
You won't have it in regular user mode.

84
